ps, and risk controls", "Practitioner Validation Check": "If dYdX’s StarkEx deployment were removed, Ethereum would lose its most prominent example of a validium-based, high-frequency financial application with off-chain DA.", "Practitioner’s Note": "This entry applies only to dYdX’s Ethereum-anchored StarkEx deployment (v3). The current Cosmos-based dYdX Chain is out of scope for this market map.", "Primary User Type": "Professional traders and institutions", "Production Usage Signal": "One of the most heavily used Ethereum-anchored validiums prior to migration", "Protocol Ownership": "Application operated by dYdX; execution engine provided by StarkWare", "Reason for Inclusion": "Implements a production validium model with explicit off-Ethereum DA, DA committee assumptions, and Ethereum-verified correctness—materially changing where DA and exit guarantees reside.", "Recovery Guarantees if DA Fails": "Limited; Ethereum verifies correctness but cannot reconstruct state without DA", "Rollup Variant": "Validium", "Security Lost vs Full Rollup": "Loss of Ethereum-guaranteed DA and forced user exits", "Settlement Layer": "Ethereum L1", "Throughput Improvements": "Very high (order-book matching and rapid settlement)", "Upgrade Authority": "Centralized — coordinated between dYdX and StarkWare", "Use-Case Fit": "Perpetuals trading, high-frequency financial markets, professional traders", "User Exit Risk": "High — users may be unable to exit positions if DA is unavailable", "What Ethereum Verifies": "Validity proofs and state commitments (not transaction or order-book data)", "Who Ultimately Controls DA": "Application operator (dYdX) within StarkWare’s DA architecture"}, "source_label": "Validiums, Volitions, and Hybrid Rollups"}'::jsonb),
